# {{backendArtifactId}} + {{frontendProjectName}}

Paired Spring Boot backend and React/Vite frontend, generated by the Menora Initializr.

## Layout

```
.
├── backend/    Spring Boot API ({{backendBootVersion}}, Java {{backendJavaVersion}})
├── frontend/   React {{frontendReactVersion}} + Vite + Feature-Slice Design
├── docker-compose.yml
└── README.md
```

## Run (local dev)

Terminal 1 — backend:

```sh
cd backend
./mvnw spring-boot:run
```

Terminal 2 — frontend:

```sh
cd frontend
{{#frontendIsPnpm}}pnpm install
pnpm dev{{/frontendIsPnpm}}{{#frontendIsNpm}}npm install
npm run dev{{/frontendIsNpm}}{{^frontendIsPnpm}}{{^frontendIsNpm}}{{frontendPackageManager}} install
{{frontendPackageManager}} run dev{{/frontendIsNpm}}{{/frontendIsPnpm}}
```

Then open <http://localhost:5173>. Calls to `/api/*` proxy to the backend on `{{apiBaseUrl}}`.

## Run (Docker)

```sh
docker compose up --build
```

## How the two halves are wired

- `frontend/.env.development` sets `VITE_API_BASE_URL={{apiBaseUrl}}`.
- `frontend/vite.config.ts` proxies `/api/*` to the same URL so the browser can hit relative paths without CORS during dev.
- `backend/src/main/java/.../config/CorsConfig.java` allows `http://localhost:5173` to call `/api/**` directly when the proxy is off (or when running the built frontend against a remote backend).

`.menora-init.json` at the root captures the full paired manifest — agents can diff it against the working tree to tell scaffold-owned files from edits.
